{"id":"civicplus-4-02042026-4442","platform":"civicplus","body":"Planning Commission","name":"2026 02 04 February PC Agena Page","date":"2026-02-04","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://www.cityofinglewood.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_02042026-4442","minutes_url":"https://www.cityofinglewood.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Minutes/_02042026-4442","packet_url":"","category_id":4,"agenda_text":"CITY OF INGLEWOOD\n  DEVELOPMENT SERVICES DEPARTMENT\n  PLANNING DIVISION\n  PLANNING COMMISSION MEETING AGENDA\nFebruary 4, 2026, 7:00 P.M.\nCity Council Chambers – Ninth Floor\n1 West Manchester Boulevard\n\n1.  Pledge of Allegiance.\n\n2.  Roll Call.\n\n3.  Communications from staff.\n\n4.  Public Comments Regarding Agenda Items. Persons wishing to address\n  the Planning Commission on any item on the agenda other than a\n  public hearing may do so at this time.\n\n5.  Minute(s) approval for December 9, 2025, and January 13, 2026,\n  Planning Commission meeting(s).\n\n6.  CONSENT ITEMS:\n  a. A six-month time limit extension for the approval of a Final\n  Planned Assembly Development (PAD) to allow 137 studio apartment\n  units on an approximately 1.55-acre MU-2 (Mixed Use-2) zoned\n  property, located at 225 North La Brea Avenue.\n\n  Recommendation:\n  Consider the staff report, any testimony and make a determination.\n  It is recommended that you:\n  1) Approve the six-month extension for SP-2021-012 and Resolution\n  No. 1987 dated April 3, 2024; or\n  2) Deny the six-month extension for SP-2021-012.\n  Item 6a Documents\n\n  b. An application by Kenrick Sanderlin, representing the City of\n  Inglewood, for the Siminski Park Improvement Project at 9717\n  Inglewood Avenue.\n\n  Recommendation:\n  Consider the staff report, any testimony and make a determination.\n  It is recommended that you:\n  1) Affirm Categorical Exemption EA-CE-2025-135 and adopt the\n  attached resolution approving PCR25-00012\n  2) Deny the request or any part thereof.\n  Item 6b Documents\n\n7.  PUBLIC HEARINGS:\n  a. A public hearing to consider an application by Erika Diaz,\n  representing the applicant, for Special Use Permit No. 25-\n  00019(SUP25-00019) to allow the sale of beer and wine for off-\n  site consumption in an approximately 2,050 square-foot one-story\n  retail tenant space that is part of a multiple tenant commercial\n  building on an MU-C (TOD Mixed Use Corridor) zoned property at\n  3535 West Imperial Highway.\n\n  A Notice of Exemption (EA-CE-2026-008) has been prepared stating\n  that the proposed project is categorically exempt from the\n  California Environmental Quality Act, a copy of which is\n  available for public review in the Planning Division office of\n  City Hall and via email request to smay@cityofinglewood.org.\n\n  Preliminary Recommendations\n  A. If the Planning Commission determines to APPROVE the request,\n  it is recommended to:\n  1) Affirm the Categorical Exemption EA-CE-2026-008;\n\f  2) Adopt the resolution approving SUP25-00019.\n  B. If the Planning Commission determines to ADD CONDITIONS, it is\n  recommended to:\n  1) Take the above actions but modify the number of conditions\n  as appropriate.\n  C. If the Planning Commission determines to DENY the request or any\n  part thereof, it is recommended to:\n  1) Take the appropriate actions and make the findings.\n  Item 7a Documents\n\n  b. A public hearing to consider an application by Raul Cueva, Jr,\n  representing IHOP, for Special Use Permit No. 25-00020(SUP25-\n  00020) to allow the sale of distilled spirits for on-site\n  consumption within an existing restaurant on a C-2A/R-3 zoned\n  property at 4410 West Century Boulevard.\n\n  A Notice of Exemption (EA-CE-2025-128) has been prepared stating\n  that the proposed project is categorically exempt from the\n  California Environmental Quality Act, a copy of which is\n  available for public review in the Planning Division office of\n  City  Hall  and  via  email  request  to\n  faith.smith@cityofinglewood.org.\n\n  Preliminary Recommendations\n  A. If the Planning Commission determines to APPROVE the request,\n  it is recommended to:\n  1) Affirm the Categorical Exemption EA-CE-2025-128;\n  2) Adopt the resolution approving SUP25-00020.\n  B. If the Planning Commission determines to ADD CONDITIONS, it is\n  recommended to:\n  1) Take the above actions but modify the number of conditions\n  as appropriate.\n  C. If the Planning Commission determines to DENY the request or any\n  part thereof, it is recommended to:\n  1) Take the appropriate actions and make the findings.\n  Item 7b Documents\n\n  c.A public hearing to consider an application by Travis Albini,\n  representing Chick-fil-A, for Special Use Permit No. 25-\n  00024(SUP25-00024) to allow a proposed 5,031 square-foot fast\n  food restaurant with a drive-through and outdoor dining within\n  a shopping center on a C-2 (General Commercial) zoned property\n  at 3003 West Manchester Boulevard.\n  This item is postponed to March 4, 2026.\n\n8.  Public Comments. Anyone wishing to address the Planning Commission\n  on any matter within their jurisdiction and not elsewhere\n  considered on the agenda may do so at this time.\n9.  Commission Initiatives.\n\n10.  Adjournment.\n\nIf you will require special accommodations, due to a disability, please\ncontact the Planning Division at (310) 412-5230, One Manchester\nBoulevard, Fourth Floor, Inglewood City Hall, Inglewood, CA 90301. All\nrequests for special accommodations must be received 48 hours prior to\nthe day of the hearing(s).\n\n\"Si no entiende esta noticia o si necesita más información, favor de\nllamar a este número (310) 412-5230.\"\n\nIn the event that the Planning Commission meeting of February 4, 2026,\nis not held, or is concluded prior to a public hearing or other agenda\nitem being considered, the public hearing or non-public hearing agenda\nitem will automatically be continued to the next regular Planning\nCommission meeting.\n\f  NEXT PLANNING COMMISSION MEETING:\n  WEDNESDAY, MARCH 4, 2026, AT 7:00 P.M.\nCITY COUNCIL CHAMBERS, NINTH FLOOR, INGLEWOOD CITY HALL\n  ONE MANCHESTER BOULEVARD\n  INGLEWOOD, CA 90301","minutes_text":"PK\u0003\u0004\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000$�\u000e��\u0001\u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000\u0013\u0000\b\u0002[Content_Types].xml �\u0004\u0002(�\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000